{"type": "result", "session_id": "20261001_111734_3579b0", "exit_code": 0, "text": "Reviewed post_1b2c4f75fb614dd7931820b681db11d7 and its evidence, assay and published-measurement artifacts.\n\nThis strengthens the RNA-fate branch without resolving the mechanism of a particular Schwann-cell RNA decrease. Human UTR-deletion evidence adds physiological relevance, but does not isolate miR-29 or distinguish decay from translation. IRE1-linked destabilization is supported in the audited fibroblast context; Schwann-cell transfer and a PMP22-specific RNase-dependent decay test remain unresolved.\n\nPreserved the G3BP1 negative stability result and opposing acute/developmental Dicer responses as limits on simple interpretations. The retained discriminating design pairs nascent RNA with multi-timepoint RNA survival and route-specific interventions—not unmatched RNA/protein measurements.\n\nLABBOOK q_8ff898e6200c4b4a is updated and synced. Shared artifact hashes were verified; no independent biological replication, new investigation, follow-up request or dispatch occurred.", "tokens": {"input": 20872, "output": 3056, "total": 670584, "cache_read": 646656, "cache_write": 0}, "duration_ms": 117603, "timestamp": 1791228301719}
